{#
/**
 * @file
 * Template for the Slate Form component.
 *
 * Renders an empty div for Slate's script to write the form into, and beside
 * it an alert naming the form, saying why it isn't there, and linking to it.
 * slate-form.js loads Slate's script.
 *
 * This template only displays what it's given, and calls nothing from a
 * module. The URLs arrive already checked: from the media item's
 * az_media_slate_form field when Canvas renders it, or from the Slate
 * formatter in the page builder. Both build them with
 * AzMediaSlateFormItem::valuesFromUrl(), from a URL that passed
 * SlateUrl::parse().
 *
 * Keep the alert outside the div. Rationale: Slate replaces everything
 * inside it. For example, if Slate can't fetch the form, it overwrites the
 * div with its own "To complete this form, click here." message, so a link
 * inside would vanish right when someone needs it. The loading spinner goes
 * inside the div for the same reason: the form replaces it.
 *
 * The link goes to the form's plain URL, not the embed URL. Slate answers the
 * embed URL with JavaScript, so a link to it would show a script instead of
 * the form.
 *
 * The alert is visible here in the markup. The loader hides it once it takes
 * over, and shows it again if the form fails, so a browser with no JavaScript
 * still gets the link. That browser is also the only one that reads the
 * reason written below, because the loader replaces it in every other case.
 *
 * The retry button ends the sentence and looks like the link below it. It's
 * a button, not a link, because it loads the form again in place instead of
 * going anywhere. It starts with the hidden attribute, and the loader shows
 * it only when the form took too long to arrive. The cause is usually a
 * slow server, such as Slate's test server waking up, and a second try often
 * works. A browser with no JavaScript never sees it, because without
 * JavaScript it couldn't do anything.
 *
 * Two openings are written and the stylesheet shows one. The plain one is for
 * a visitor, and names neither Slate nor the form, because neither means
 * anything to them. The loader asks for the named one, by adding
 * --names-form, when the reason is something a person can act on.
 *
 * Props:
 * - form.embed_url: The URL Slate answers with its embed script. The loader
 *   adds the div parameter, and points Slate at the container's id.
 * - form.canonical_url: The form's plain URL, safe to link to.
 * - form.label: The media item's name. The placeholder filter puts it in as
 *   Drupal's own em.placeholder, so the sentence stays one translatable
 *   string, and the loader can read the name back out of that element.
 *
 * Renders nothing without an embed URL. For example, an editor has placed
 * the component in Canvas but hasn't picked a form yet.
 */
#}
{% set attributes = attributes|default(create_attribute()) %}
{% set embed_url = form.embed_url|default('') %}
{% set canonical_url = form.canonical_url|default('') %}
{% set label = form.label|default('') %}

{% if embed_url %}
  <div{{ attributes.addClass('az-media-slate') }}>
    <div class="az-media-slate__form" data-az-slate-embed-src="{{ embed_url }}"></div>
    <div class="az-media-slate__fallback alert alert-warning" role="alert">
      <p class="az-media-slate__message">
        <span class="az-media-slate__icon" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</span>
        <span class="az-media-slate__opening az-media-slate__opening--plain">{{ 'A form couldn\'t load'|t }}</span>
        <span class="az-media-slate__opening az-media-slate__opening--named">{% trans %}The Slate form {{ label|placeholder }} was not embedded{% endtrans %}</span>
        <span class="az-media-slate__reason">{{ 'because this browser has JavaScript turned off.'|t }}</span>
        <button type="button" class="az-media-slate__retry alert-link" hidden>
          {{- 'Try again'|t }}
          <svg class="az-media-slate__link-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
               viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
               stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
               aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <polyline points="23 4 23 10 17 10"/>
            <path d="M20.49 15a9 9 0 1 1-2.12-9.36L23 10"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </p>
      <a href="{{ canonical_url }}" class="az-media-slate__link alert-link" rel="noopener">
        {{ 'Open the form'|t }}
        <svg class="az-media-slate__link-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
             viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
             stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
             aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"/>
          <polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"/>
          <line x1="10" y1="14" x2="21" y2="3"/>
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endif %}
